# Alphabetical, with Main.lua last, and that is the whole of the ordering. Every file under
# src/ does one thing when the client executes it — hang a `ns.newThing` factory off the
# namespace — and nothing calls another module's factory until Main.lua wires them together,
# so the client is free to read them in any order. Sorted rather than appended-to because an
# append is where two unrelated branches meet: a list in the order features arrived in puts
# every new one on the same line, and git merges by line locality (issue #155).
#
# If a file ever needs another to have run first, that is a reason to move the work into
# Main.lua rather than a reason to move the line.

